  "result": "Perfect! All **477 tests pass**. The dashboard implementation is complete. Here's a summary:\n\n## Dashboard Implementation Summary\n\n**Feature**: The `dashboard(invoices, asOf)` function provides a comprehensive summary of invoice data.\n\n**Function Signature**:\n```javascript\ndashboard(invoices, asOf) \u2192 {\n  counts: { draft, issued, partially_paid, paid },\n  outstanding: number,\n  overdue: { count, amount },\n  topCustomers: [{ customerId, due }, ...]\n}\n```\n\n**Implementation Details**:\n\n1. **Counts** - Number of invoices per status (draft, issued, partially_paid, paid)\n\n2. **Outstanding** - Total amount still due on invoices with status 'issued' or 'partially_paid'\n\n3. **Overdue** - Object with:\n   - `count`: Number of overdue invoices\n   - `amount`: Total amount of overdue invoices (from overdueInvoices function)\n\n4. **Top Customers** - Top 3 customers by amount still due, formatted as `[{ customerId, due }, ...]` with highest amounts first\n\n**Key Features**:\n- Normalizes customer IDs (trim, uppercase) for consistent grouping\n- Aggregates multiple invoices per customer\n- Filters invoices by status appropriately\n- Excludes draft invoices from outstanding/overdue calculations\n- Correctly handles partially paid invoices\n\n**Test Coverage - 16 New Tests**:\n- Empty invoices handling\n- Status counting accuracy\n- Outstanding calculation\n- Overdue tracking\n- Top 3 customers ranking\n- Multiple invoices per customer aggregation\n- Customer ID normalization\n- Mixed status scenarios\n- Edge cases (zero due amounts, future invoices)\n- Data structure validation\n\n**Test Results**: \u2713 **477/477 tests passing** (460 previous + 17 new dashboard tests)",
